# run-suites.quarantine -- suites allowed to fail without reddening the
# required check that bin/run-suites.sh gates (see #316).
#
# One entry per line, tab-separated: <suite-path>\t<issue-ref>\t<reason>
# The suite still runs and a failure still prints loud (::warning, not
# silence) -- quarantine hides a failure from the gate, not from the log.
# Remove the line the moment the suite is fixed; a quarantine entry for a
# now-passing suite prints its own stale notice so it does not linger.
#
# This file exists so the NEXT suite that goes bad under time pressure has a
# one-line lever instead of forcing the choice #125 forced -- block every PR
# in the repo, or drop the whole `suites` required check.
